{
  "name": "destructive",
  "stopOnError": false,
  "destructive": true,
  "notes": [
    "The LLM block switches to builder mode first: delete-backend now lives in LlmBackendCard's builderActions snippet, absent in the operator default this script boots into.",
    "llm-empty-add-btn is reached through a stub, not through deletions: LlmBackendRepository::delete refuses the default backend (crates/apollia-core/src/llm_backend.rs:432, CannotDeleteDefault, mapped to 409 at apollia-runtime routes_llm/backends.rs:150) and set-default only moves the flag, so a table with one backend can never be emptied from the UI. The block arms stubInvoke list_llm_backends resolve [] (an empty array, no backend type to drift), clicks llm-reload-btn so the route's own refresh() (routes/Llm.svelte:44-50, 85) writes [] into the sse llmBackends store (the 10 s watchdog of sse.ts:709 would do it too, hence the 25 s waits), plays llm-empty-add-btn (routes/Llm.svelte:130) into llm-backend-dialog, cancels, clears the stub, reloads again for the real list, and re-enters Settings > LLM so the model-hub step that follows finds the settings page it expects.",
    "One uninstall of apollia-guide serves agent-uninstall-confirm, the five companion-error-* anchors and agent-unavailable-install: rows are addressed by agents-search then agent-list-row nth 0 (store order, no sort, Agents.svelte:107; the expect on agent-detail-title guards the row), never nth -1. Uninstall unregisters the guide (commands/agents/lifecycle.rs:240-248) and it is re-provisioned only at boot (main.rs:171), so create_companion_session rejects GuideAgentNotInstalled (commands/onboarding/companion.rs:95-102); the message carries none of timeout/network/connect/session, so the error is kind internal / ERR_COMPANION_UNKNOWN (stores/companion.ts:183-220) and the details toggle renders on error.message (CompanionErrorState.svelte:121). companion-error-settings maps internal to the settings route with the panel left mounted (CompanionPanel.svelte:328-340); companion-error-close hides it, the store's enabled stays true, so no later step toggles the companion.",
    "agent-unavailable-install: seed-session-2 is an agent-mode session on apollia-guide (tests/cli/seed/fragments/chat.sql:39-42); it is opened through the palette's Sessions group (paletteIndex.ts:98-124, keywords carry the session id; the group lists the freshest chatSessions when no session was touched through the palette yet, recentSessionsStore.ts:53-66) so the banner condition of ChatConversation.svelte:142-147 holds with the guide gone from $agents. The mapper's seed-classifier route is refuted: seed-classifier is a worker and Agents.svelte:107 keeps workers out of agent-list-row.",
    "provider-delete-confirm-confirm runs before the project section deletes seed-project-alpha (the project that owns every seeded provider, projects.sql). It removes seed-provider-alpha-rules; ProviderEditDialog's save carries no testid, so there is no deterministic way back, which is why it lives here and never in master-det.",
    "update-install-btn stays unplayed and a boundary even in this book: it renders only on phase available (UpdateCheckPanel.svelte:184), which needs a signed latest.json from the GitHub endpoint of tauri.conf.json (commands/updates.rs:130-141, offline the check fails at transport), and acting on it runs install_update, which replaces the binary and restarts the app before the report is written.",
    "agent-detail-title is a prop value (AgentDetailHeader.svelte:154 titleTestid, applied at lib/components/operator/DetailHeader.svelte:44), invisible to the validator's literal corpus; declared dynamic here exactly as agents-det declares it.",
    "user-menu-quit is played last with quit_app answered by a stub: the real command exits the process before the report is written, so the gesture is exercised up to the IPC call and the window is asserted still alive afterwards."
  ],
